      "On the one hand, it is undeniable that historical industrialization relied heavily on fossil fuels, deforestation, and unrestricted resource extraction. Developing nations rightly point out that wealthier countries built their prosperity through carbon-intensive growth, and that millions of citizens still require reliable electricity, modern infrastructure, and decent employment to achieve basic human dignity. Consequently, any environmental agenda that demands economic stagnation or ignores developmental justice is both morally indefensible and politically doomed to fail.",
